  "title": "Coast Guard Aircrew Hoists Ill Cruise Ship Passenger",
  "description": "A Coast Guard helicopter crew from Air Station Clearwater, Fla., medically evacuated a 67-year-old woman from the cruise ship Carnival Fantasy 80 miles east of Ponce De Leon Inlet, Fla., Friday, Aug. 29, 2014 after she began experiencing symptoms consistent with previous medical complications. The aircrew hoisted the woman off the cruise ship and transferred her, her husband and a nurse to UF Health Jacksonville in Jacksonville, Fla. (U.S. Coast Guard video)",
